        <div id="warranty-returns" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">7. ANCHEER Warranty, Returns and Support</h2>
<p>
            The TR6056 listing, as OCDevel recorded it, offers a one-year manufacturer warranty described as a
            "365-day service-first warranty". We found no published ANCHEER warranty document for treadmills,
            and no ANCHEER address or phone number for treadmill support. In practice that means three things.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Your first protection is Amazon’s return window.</strong> On a listing sold by Amazon.com,
            Amazon’s own return policy applies, and Amazon handles a return of a faulty pad in the first weeks.
            On a listing sold by a third party, the seller sets the terms. Run the pad through its full speed
            range and fold it a few times in the first days, so that any fault surfaces while a return is easy.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Warranty claims go through the seller.</strong> After the return window, a claim means
            contacting the seller through your Amazon order. Keep the order confirmation, take a video of the
            fault, and expect to be offered a part rather than a replacement machine.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Consider who will supply parts in three years.</strong> A brand with a website and a parts
            store can sell you a belt or a motor board long after the warranty ends. A marketplace brand whose
            listing has disappeared usually cannot. For a $160 pad that may be an acceptable risk. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-warranty-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">warranty guide</a> and
            <a href="/how-long-do-walking-pads-last/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how long walking pads last</a>
            help you weigh it.
          </p>
